      "side": 1,
      "message": "You cannot preemptively protect the ABI from CRC changes like this because it\u0027s too late, those types are *already* part of the CRC calculation (whether as full definitions or just as forward declarations).\n\nIf / when changes to those type land *and* those type changes are audited to be ABI safe, then you can use macros to hide the changes from `genksyms`. Similarly, if new includes are needed which pull definitions into new source files, affecting CRCs, they too can be hidden.",
